From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: InSnh-Gd <2479955131@qq.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 16:54:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] anv: name the ICD entry point for a link beside another
 driver

Stela links Mesa's Vulkan drivers into the boot image rather than loading them
through a loader, and two drivers define the loader interface's
vk_icdGetInstanceProcAddr: one link cannot hold both. Under STELA_LIBC, which
only that image's units define, the Intel driver's definition carries Stela's
own name; the shared library keeps the loader's.
---
 src/intel/vulkan/anv_instance.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/intel/vulkan/anv_instance.c b/src/intel/vulkan/anv_instance.c
index c25e66acdb5a94ad454a15f11aba969970b9561a..bf2ce82d4c898d4c33c70f22df09d207e87809c0 100644
--- a/src/intel/vulkan/anv_instance.c
+++ b/src/intel/vulkan/anv_instance.c
@@ -309,6 +309,14 @@ PFN_vkVoidFunction anv_GetInstanceProcAddr(
 /* With version 1+ of the loader interface the ICD should expose
  * vk_icdGetInstanceProcAddr to work around certain LD_PRELOAD issues seen in apps.
  */
+/* Stela links Mesa's drivers into the boot image instead of loading them
+ * through a loader, so two of them share one link and each one's loader
+ * interface name would collide. The Intel driver's carries Stela's own name
+ * there; NVK's keeps the loader's.
+ */
+#ifdef STELA_LIBC
+#define vk_icdGetInstanceProcAddr stela_anv_icd_get_instance_proc_addr
+#endif
 PUBLIC
 VKAPI_ATTR PFN_vkVoidFunction VKAPI_CALL vk_icdGetInstanceProcAddr(
     VkInstance                                  instance,
